'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-so9-dac-mode-adc-enable.spin2
''   Purpose.... Decide prediction SO9 on SILICON: does OUT switch the ADC in a DAC smart-pin mode with TT = %00
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 26 Sep 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED (brief BRIEF-SO9, Parts 2 and 5)
    The published %TT table (P2 Documentation, p2-documentation.txt
    :7652-7657) says, for the smart-pin modes:
      "for all smart pin modes (%SSSSS > %00000):
         x0 = output disabled, regardless of DIR
         x1 = output enabled, regardless of DIR
       for DAC smart pin modes (%SSSSS = %00001..%00011):
         0x = OUT enables ADC in DAC_MODE, M[7:0] overridden"
    Read as published, TT = %00 in a DAC smart mode is a pin whose output is
    off and whose ADC is switched by OUT.
    Prediction under test (an independent reading of the logic): with TT
    bit 0 clear, raising OUT runs NOTHING -- the ADC never runs. With TT bit 0
    set, OUT runs the ADC as published, and the fast DAC is on and drives the
    pin while it does. Nobody has observed this on a part; this program is
    written to be able to show it WRONG, and the published table says it is.

  RIG
    Any P2 board, NOTHING attached to P4 or P5 (the run sheet keeps P0..P7
    free). Pin P = PIN_P = 4 (the pin under test) and P+1 = PIN_NBR = 5 (the
    observer). Change PIN_P in the CON block to move the pair; PIN_P must be
    0..30 so that P+1 is in INA. Pin P is DRIVEN by the fast DAC whenever TT
    bit 0 is set (C1, C2) and as a plain output in the path control -- do not
    choose a pin the board uses for anything else.

  DEBUGGER (EF-057)
    DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001: the debug interrupt lives in cog 0 only. Every
    pin operation and every INA read runs in a dedicated PASM cog started by
    COGINIT from the DAT block below; cog 0 only checks constants, reads the
    hub mailbox and reports.

  CONFIGURATION WORDS, FIELD BY FIELD (published fields only)
    WRPIN D layout (p2-documentation.txt:7572):
      D = %AAAA_BBBB_FFF_MMMMMMMMMMMMM_TT_SSSSS_0
          [31:28] [27:24] [23:21] [20:8] [7:6] [5:1] [0]
    ("The M[12:0] bits within the WRPIN instruction's D[20:8] operand go
    directly to these bits", :7865-7866.)

    Pin P, TT = %00:  $0014_0002 = %0000_0000_000_1010000000000_00_00001_0
      %AAAA  = %0000  this pin's read state (:7578; unused by these modes)
      %BBBB  = %0000
      %FFF   = %000   A, B (:7604)
      %M     = %1_0100_0000_0000 (D[20] and D[18] set)
               M[12:10] = %101 -> "'DAC_MODE' is enabled when
                          M[12:10] = %101" (:7638)
               M[9:8]   = %00  -> Spin2 v55 P_DAC_990R_3V "DAC 990 ohm,
                          3.3V peak, ADC 1x -> IN" (spin2-v55-text.txt:1476)
               M[7:0]   = 0    -> "M[7:0] overridden" in the DAC smart modes
                          (:7656; :7903 "overrides M[7:0] to feed the pin's
                          8-bit DAC pseudo-random data")
      %TT    = %00    -> x0 "output disabled, regardless of DIR" (:7653);
                         0x "OUT enables ADC in DAC_MODE" (:7656)
      %SSSSS = %00001 -> "DAC noise" with M[12:10] = %101 (:7685-7691,
                         :7902); needs no WXPIN/WYPIN setup
      bit 0  = 0      (layout :7572)
    Pin P, TT = %01:  $0014_0042 = the word above with D[6] set
      %TT    = %01    -> x1 "output enabled, regardless of DIR" (:7654);
                         0x "OUT enables ADC in DAC_MODE" (:7656)
    Pin P+1:          $7000_0000 = %0111_0000_000_0000000000000_00_00000_0
      %AAAA  = %0111  0xxx "true" (:7576), x111 "relative -1 pin's read
                      state" (:7585) -> A = pin P's read state
      %FFF   = %000   "A, B"; "The resultant 'A' will drive the IN signal
                      in non-smart-pin modes" (:7604, :7615)
      %M     = 0      Spin2 v55 P_LOGIC_A (default) "Logic level A -> IN,
                      output OUT" (spin2-v55-text.txt:1456)
      %TT    = %00, %SSSSS = %00000: smart pin off, "DIR enables output"
                      (:7640-7641); DIR stays LOW -> P+1 never drives.
    Cross-check, from the Spin2 v55 symbol table (spin2-v55-text.txt:1432,
    :1456, :1476, :1521-1522, :1529, :1531):
      $0014_0002 = P_DAC_990R_3V | P_TT_00 | P_DAC_NOISE
      $0014_0042 = P_DAC_990R_3V | P_TT_01 | P_DAC_NOISE   (P_TT_01 = P_OE)
      $7000_0000 = P_MINUS1_A | P_LOGIC_A | P_TT_00 | P_NORMAL
    Cog 0 decodes all three words into these fields at run time, prints
    them, and gates on them and on the symbol compositions (control W).

  OBSERVABLE
    Pin P's own IN is not read. Pin P+1, configured with $7000_0000 and
    DIR low, carries pin P's read state on its IN, which is bit P+1 of INA.
    One SAMPLE = 4096 consecutive reads of INA in a REP loop (6 clocks per
    read, 24,576 clocks), counting the reads in which bit P+1 = 1.

  SEQUENCE (measuring cog; brief Part 5)
    once   : P+1: DIRL, WRPIN $7000_0000, OUTL (DIR stays low all run)
    K pre  : path control (below)
    5 rounds, each C1, C2, C3, C4 in that order. For each condition:
             DIRL P; WRPIN P with the word; DIRH P; OUTL or OUTH P (set
             explicitly, whatever the previous condition left); WAITX
             SETTLE_CLK (10,000 >= the brief's 1000 clocks); one sample.
      C1 : $0014_0042 (TT = %01), OUT low   brief: fast DAC on, ADC off
      C2 : $0014_0042 (TT = %01), OUT high  brief: fast DAC on, ADC on
      C3 : $0014_0002 (TT = %00), OUT low   brief: nothing on
      C4 : $0014_0002 (TT = %00), OUT high  brief: nothing on (the defect)
                                            table: ADC on, output off
    K post : path control again
    end    : both pins DIRL, WRPIN #0, OUTL (smart pin off, output released)

  CONTROLS (gating -- a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT)
    W : PIN_P in 0..30; each configuration word decodes to the fields
        above and equals its Spin2 symbol composition.
    K : path control, before AND after the rounds. Pin P as a plain pin
        (WRPIN #0): DRVH -> P+1 must read 4096 of 4096; DRVL -> 0 of 4096.
        Proves the observer sees pin P's read state and the sampler counts
        every read. Fails if something is attached to P or P+1.
    T : the measuring cog reports done within RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC.
    The brief's own control -- C2 separates from C1 -- is NOT a rig gate: its
    failure is the brief's INCONCLUSIVE outcome, reported as such.

  PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run; printed by the program)
    X SEPARATES from Y when every sample of X lies outside the range from
    the smallest to the largest sample of Y (brief Part 5).
    Control : C2 separates from C1 -- the reading sees the ADC at TT = %01.
    CONFIRMED    : C2 sep C1, C4 does NOT sep C3, C4 sep C2.
                   OUT does nothing at TT = %00; what TT = %00 with OUT high
                   produces is not the running ADC.
    REFUTED      : C2 sep C1, C4 sep C3, C4 does NOT sep C2.
                   OUT runs the ADC at TT = %00, as the published %TT table
                   states; the brief's reading is wrong.
    INCONCLUSIVE : C2 does NOT sep C1 (the reading does not show the ADC,
                   whatever C3 and C4 show); or C2 sep C1 and C4 sep BOTH C3
                   and C2 (a pattern neither side predicts); or C2 sep C1 and
                   C4 sep NEITHER (the ranges do not discriminate).
    C1 and C3 (OUT low) measure what pin P's read state carries with the ADC
    off.
    The brief marks that UNDETERMINED; no value is predicted, the samples
    are printed in their own section.

  DEPENDS ON CLAIMS THE BRIEF MARKS UNDETERMINED
    - what the pin's read state carries in the DAC state with the ADC off:
      measured (C1, C3), never assumed; the verdict compares samples only
      with each other.
    - whether the ADC's decision stream in this state holds both values: if
      it sits at the ADC-off value, C2 does not separate from C1 and the run
      is INCONCLUSIVE, not a refutation.
    - whether the fast DAC's drive is visible through an external load: not
      relied on (nothing is attached).

  DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF'S STEP LIST
    Each condition issues DIRL before its WRPIN. The brief's step list is
    WRPIN, DIRH, OUT. P2 Documentation :7855 says "A smart pin should be
    configured while its DIR bit is low, holding it in reset", so every
    condition starts from a smart-pin reset and no condition's state carries
    into the next through the running smart pin. OUT is still set after
    DIRH, as the brief orders it.

  VERIFIED OPCODES AND DATA (pnut-ts -d -l v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read
  from the .lst hub image; object offsets, cog addresses in brackets)
    CON values in the symbol table: CFG_DAC_TT00 = SYM_DAC_TT00 = $0014_0002,
      CFG_DAC_TT01 = SYM_DAC_TT01 = $0014_0042, CFG_NBR = SYM_NBR = $7000_0000.
    DAT longs: $118 [$035] cfg_tt00_ = $0014_0002   $11C [$036] cfg_tt01_
      = $0014_0042   $120 [$037] cfg_nbr_ = $7000_0000   $124 [$038] reads_
      = $0000_1000 (4096)
    wrpin cfg_nbr_, #5     $FC046E05  1100000 0LI: L=0 D=$037, I=1 S=#5
    wrpin cfg_, #4         $FC047204  L=0 D=$039 (cfg_), I=1 S=#4
    wrpin #0, #4 / #0, #5  $FC0C0004 / $FC0C0005  L=1 I=1
    mov cfg_, cfg_tt01_    $F6007236  (C1/C2)   mov cfg_, cfg_tt00_ $F6007235 (C3/C4)
    dirl #4 / dirh #4      $FD640840 / $FD640841
    outl #4 / outh #4      if_z $AD640848 / if_nz $5D640849 (after cmp outlvl_,#0 wz
                           $F20C7400)
    drvh #4 / drvl #4      $FD640859 / $FD640858 (path control)
    dirl #5 / outl #5      $FD640A40 / $FD640A48 (observer, DIR low all run)
    waitx ##10000          AUGD $FF800013 + $FD66201F
    rep #3, reads_         $FCD80638  1100110 1LI: L=1 D=#3, I=0 S=$038 (reads_)
    mov insnap_, ina       $F6007BFE  S=$1FE (INA as the S operand)
    testb insnap_, #5 wc   $F4147A05  C=1, I=1, S=#5 (bit P+1)
    if_c add count_, #1    $C1047801
    wrlong count_, ptrb    $FC647980  S=$180 (PTRB)
    wrlong #1, ptra        $FC6C0300  done flag, after both pins are cleared

  HOW TO RUN
    Compile: pnut-ts -d test-so9-dac-mode-adc-enable.spin2
    Load to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10). The
    engine runs about 5 ms; the report prints about 70 lines. Done when you
    see one "VERDICT: ..." line (or "NO VERDICT"), then "=== END ===" and
    DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq          = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS        = %0000_0001        ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  PIN_P             = 4                 ' pin under test (DAC smart mode)
  PIN_NBR           = PIN_P + 1         ' observer pin: A input = relative -1 pin = PIN_P
  PIN_P_MIN         = 0
  PIN_P_MAX         = 30                ' PIN_NBR must be a pin of INA (0..31)

  ROUNDS            = 5                 ' C1..C4 in order, five times over
  READS_PER_SAMPLE  = 4096              ' INA reads per sample
  SETTLE_CLK        = 10_000            ' WAITX after every change (brief: >= 1000)
  RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC   = 2                 ' host wait cap; the engine runs about 5 ms
  MBOX_DONE         = 1                 ' mailbox[MB_DONE] once the pins are safe

  ' plain-pin path control: expected counts of P+1 = 1 out of READS_PER_SAMPLE
  K_HIGH_EXPECT     = READS_PER_SAMPLE  ' pin P driven high
  K_LOW_EXPECT      = 0                 ' pin P driven low

  ' OUT level the measuring cog sets on pin P for a condition
  OUT_LOW           = 0
  OUT_HIGH          = 1

CON ' ---- Configuration Words ----
  ' the brief's words (derivation in the header)
  CFG_DAC_TT00      = $0014_0002        ' DAC_MODE, DAC noise, TT = %00
  CFG_DAC_TT01      = $0014_0042        ' DAC_MODE, DAC noise, TT = %01
  CFG_NBR           = $7000_0000        ' A = relative -1 pin's read state, smart off
  ' the same words composed from the Spin2 v55 symbols (control W)
  SYM_DAC_TT00      = P_DAC_990R_3V | P_TT_00 | P_DAC_NOISE
  SYM_DAC_TT01      = P_DAC_990R_3V | P_TT_01 | P_DAC_NOISE
  SYM_NBR           = P_MINUS1_A | P_LOGIC_A | P_TT_00 | P_NORMAL

  ' WRPIN D field positions and widths (p2-documentation.txt:7572)
  SHIFT_AAAA        = 28
  MASK_AAAA         = %1111
  SHIFT_BBBB        = 24
  MASK_BBBB         = %1111
  SHIFT_FFF         = 21
  MASK_FFF          = %111
  SHIFT_M           = 8
  MASK_M            = %1_1111_1111_1111
  SHIFT_M_TOP       = 10                ' M[12:10] within M
  MASK_M_TOP        = %111
  SHIFT_TT          = 6
  MASK_TT           = %11
  SHIFT_SSSSS       = 1
  MASK_SSSSS        = %1_1111
  MASK_BIT0         = 1

  ' expected field values
  AAAA_THIS_PIN     = %0000             ' true, this pin's read state
  AAAA_MINUS1       = %0111             ' true, relative -1 pin's read state
  BBBB_DEFAULT      = %0000
  FFF_PASS_AB       = %000
  M_DAC_990R        = %1_0100_0000_0000 ' M[12:10] = %101 DAC_MODE, M[9:0] = 0
  M_LOGIC_A         = 0                 ' logic level A -> IN
  TT_OUTPUT_OFF     = %00               ' smart modes: x0 = output disabled
  TT_OUTPUT_ON      = %01               ' smart modes: x1 = output enabled
  SSSSS_OFF         = %00000            ' smart pin off
  SSSSS_DAC_NOISE   = %00001            ' DAC noise (with DAC_MODE)
  BIT0_REQUIRED     = 0

CON ' ---- Mailbox Layout ----
  ' Conditions, in run order within a round:
  '  COND_C1 - TT = %01, OUT low
  '  COND_C2 - TT = %01, OUT high
  '  COND_C3 - TT = %00, OUT low
  '  COND_C4 - TT = %00, OUT high
  #0, COND_C1, COND_C2, COND_C3, COND_C4
  COND_COUNT        = 4

  ' mailbox longs, in the order the measuring cog writes them:
  '  MB_DONE      - MBOX_DONE once the engine has finished and released the pins
  '  MB_K_PRE_HI  - path control before the rounds, pin P driven high
  '  MB_K_PRE_LO  - path control before the rounds, pin P driven low
  '  MB_SAMPLES   - ROUNDS * COND_COUNT samples, round-major, C1..C4 per round
  '  MB_K_POST_HI - path control after the rounds, pin P driven high
  '  MB_K_POST_LO - path control after the rounds, pin P driven low
  MB_DONE           = 0
  MB_K_PRE_HI       = 1
  MB_K_PRE_LO       = 2
  MB_SAMPLES        = 3
  MB_K_POST_HI      = MB_SAMPLES + ROUNDS * COND_COUNT
  MB_K_POST_LO      = MB_K_POST_HI + 1
  MB_LONGS          = MB_K_POST_LO + 1

VAR ' ---- Mailbox & Analysis State ----
  long mailbox[MB_LONGS]                ' written by the measuring cog
  long sample_min[COND_COUNT]           ' smallest sample per condition
  long sample_max[COND_COUNT]           ' largest sample per condition
  long fail_count                       ' gating control failures


PUB main() | engineCog, startTick
'' Run the SO9 rig: check the constants and configuration words, start the
'' measuring cog, wait for its done flag, then print every sample and the verdict.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local engineCog - cog id COGINIT returned (negative = no free cog)
' @local startTick - CT when the wait for the done flag began

  longfill(@mailbox, 0, MB_LONGS)
  fail_count := 0
  debug("=== SO9: in a DAC smart-pin mode, does OUT switch the ADC when TT = %00? ===")
  debug("pin P = ", udec_(PIN_P), " (under test), P+1 = ", udec_(PIN_NBR), " (observer, DIR low); ", udec_(READS_PER_SAMPLE), " INA reads per sample; settle ", udec_(SETTLE_CLK), " clocks; ", udec_(ROUNDS), " rounds")
  print_predictions()
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- CONTROL W: configuration words, decoded into the published WRPIN fields ---")
  check_rig_constants()
  if fail_count <> 0
    debug("NO VERDICT: a construction control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the measuring cog was not started")
  else
    engineCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @engine, @mailbox)
    if engineCog < 0
      debug("RIG FAIL: no free cog for the measuring engine")
      debug("NO VERDICT: nothing was measured")
    else
      startTick := getct()
      repeat until mailbox[MB_DONE] == MBOX_DONE or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq * RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC
      if mailbox[MB_DONE] <> MBOX_DONE
        cogstop(engineCog)
        pinclear(PIN_P addpins 1)
        debug("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not report done within ", udec_(RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC), " s (expected about 5 ms); pins P and P+1 cleared by cog 0")
        debug("NO VERDICT: the measurement did not complete")
      else
        debug("measuring cog = ", udec_(engineCog), " (debugger restricted to cog 0)")
        report()
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("=== END ===")
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat


PRI print_predictions()
' Print the outcomes fixed before the run, and the rule that decides them.
'

  debug("PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run):")
  debug("  X SEPARATES from Y when every sample of X lies outside [smallest Y sample, largest Y sample]")
  debug("  C1 TT=%01 OUT low | C2 TT=%01 OUT high | C3 TT=%00 OUT low | C4 TT=%00 OUT high")
  debug("  control     : C2 separates from C1 (the reading sees the ADC at TT = %01); if not -> INCONCLUSIVE whatever C3/C4 show")
  debug("  prediction  : C4 does NOT separate from C3, and C4 separates from C2  -> VERDICT: CONFIRMED")
  debug("  published   : %TT table, TT = %00 -> 'OUT enables ADC in DAC_MODE' (p2-documentation.txt:7652-7657)")
  debug("                C4 separates from C3, and C4 does NOT separate from C2  -> VERDICT: REFUTED")
  debug("  C4 separates from both C3 and C2 (unpredicted pattern)                -> VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE")
  debug("  C4 separates from neither C3 nor C2 (ranges do not discriminate)      -> VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE")
  debug("  C1 and C3 (OUT low, ADC off): undetermined -- measured and printed, no value predicted")
  debug("  path control K (pin P a plain pin, before and after): P+1 reads ", udec_(K_HIGH_EXPECT), " driven high, ", udec_(K_LOW_EXPECT), " driven low, else RIG FAIL / NO VERDICT")


PRI check_rig_constants()
' Control W: the pin pair lies in INA, and every configuration word decodes
' to the published fields and equals its Spin2 symbol composition.
'

  if PIN_P < PIN_P_MIN or PIN_P > PIN_P_MAX
    debug("RIG FAIL: PIN_P = ", sdec_(PIN_P), " must be ", udec_(PIN_P_MIN), "..", udec_(PIN_P_MAX), " so that P+1 is a pin of INA")
    fail_count++
  check_word(string("pin P TT=%00"), CFG_DAC_TT00, SYM_DAC_TT00, AAAA_THIS_PIN, M_DAC_990R, TT_OUTPUT_OFF, SSSSS_DAC_NOISE)
  check_word(string("pin P TT=%01"), CFG_DAC_TT01, SYM_DAC_TT01, AAAA_THIS_PIN, M_DAC_990R, TT_OUTPUT_ON, SSSSS_DAC_NOISE)
  check_word(string("pin P+1     "), CFG_NBR, SYM_NBR, AAAA_MINUS1, M_LOGIC_A, TT_OUTPUT_OFF, SSSSS_OFF)


PRI check_word(pLabel, cfgWord, symWord, expAaaa, expMode, expTt, expSssss) | fldAaaa, fldBbbb, fldFff, fldMode, fldTt, fldSssss, fldBit0
' Decode one WRPIN word into its published fields, print them, and count a
' construction failure if any field or the symbol composition disagrees.
'
' @param pLabel - label string for the printed line
' @param cfgWord - the configuration word the measuring cog writes
' @param symWord - the same word composed from the Spin2 v55 symbols
' @param expAaaa - expected %AAAA
' @param expMode - expected %M (13 bits)
' @param expTt - expected %TT
' @param expSssss - expected %SSSSS

' Local Variables:
' @local fldAaaa - decoded %AAAA
' @local fldBbbb - decoded %BBBB
' @local fldFff - decoded %FFF
' @local fldMode - decoded %M (13 bits)
' @local fldTt - decoded %TT
' @local fldSssss - decoded %SSSSS
' @local fldBit0 - decoded bit 0

  fldAaaa := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_AAAA) & MASK_AAAA
  fldBbbb := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_BBBB) & MASK_BBBB
  fldFff := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_FFF) & MASK_FFF
  fldMode := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_M) & MASK_M
  fldTt := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_TT) & MASK_TT
  fldSssss := (cfgWord >> SHIFT_SSSSS) & MASK_SSSSS
  fldBit0 := cfgWord & MASK_BIT0
  debug("  ", zstr_(pLabel), " ", uhex_long_(cfgWord), ": AAAA=", ubin_(fldAaaa), " BBBB=", ubin_(fldBbbb), " FFF=", ubin_(fldFff), " M=", ubin_(fldMode), " (M[12:10]=", ubin_((fldMode >> SHIFT_M_TOP) & MASK_M_TOP), ") TT=", ubin_(fldTt), " SSSSS=", ubin_(fldSssss), " bit0=", udec_(fldBit0), "  symbols=", uhex_long_(symWord))
  if fldAaaa <> expAaaa or fldBbbb <> BBBB_DEFAULT or fldFff <> FFF_PASS_AB or fldMode <> expMode or fldTt <> expTt or fldSssss <> expSssss or fldBit0 <> BIT0_REQUIRED
    debug("RIG FAIL: ", zstr_(pLabel), " fields differ from the expected AAAA=", ubin_(expAaaa), " M=", ubin_(expMode), " TT=", ubin_(expTt), " SSSSS=", ubin_(expSssss), " (BBBB, FFF, bit0 zero)")
    fail_count++
  if cfgWord <> symWord
    debug("RIG FAIL: ", zstr_(pLabel), " word ", uhex_long_(cfgWord), " differs from its Spin2 symbol composition ", uhex_long_(symWord))
    fail_count++


PRI report() | bContinue
' Print the path controls and every raw sample, then gate, then run the
' separation tests and print the verdict. Single exit.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local bContinue - TRUE while every gating control has passed

  debug(" ")
  debug("--- CONTROL K: neighbour path (pin P a plain pin, WRPIN #0) ---")
  check_path_controls()
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- RAW SAMPLES (count of reads with INA bit P+1 = 1, of ", udec_(READS_PER_SAMPLE), ") ---")
  print_samples()
  compute_ranges()
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- RANGES ---")
  print_ranges()
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- ADC-OFF READINGS (OUT low; the brief marks the value undetermined) ---")
  print_adc_off()
  debug(" ")
  bContinue := (fail_count == 0)
  if bContinue == FALSE
    debug("NO VERDICT: a rig control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the samples are printed for diagnosis only")
  else
    decide_verdict()


PRI check_path_controls()
' Control K: pin P driven high then low as a plain pin, before and after the
' rounds; P+1 must read every read high, then every read low.
'

  debug("  before rounds: P high -> ", udec_(mailbox[MB_K_PRE_HI]), "   P low -> ", udec_(mailbox[MB_K_PRE_LO]))
  debug("  after rounds : P high -> ", udec_(mailbox[MB_K_POST_HI]), "   P low -> ", udec_(mailbox[MB_K_POST_LO]))
  debug("  expected     : P high -> ", udec_(K_HIGH_EXPECT), "   P low -> ", udec_(K_LOW_EXPECT))
  if mailbox[MB_K_PRE_HI] <> K_HIGH_EXPECT or mailbox[MB_K_PRE_LO] <> K_LOW_EXPECT
    debug("RIG FAIL: path control before the rounds -- P+1 does not follow pin P driven as a plain pin")
    fail_count++
  if mailbox[MB_K_POST_HI] <> K_HIGH_EXPECT or mailbox[MB_K_POST_LO] <> K_LOW_EXPECT
    debug("RIG FAIL: path control after the rounds -- P+1 does not follow pin P driven as a plain pin")
    fail_count++


PRI sample_at(roundIdx, condIdx) : readCount
' One recorded sample.
'
' @param roundIdx - round, 0..ROUNDS-1
' @param condIdx - condition, COND_C1..COND_C4
' @returns readCount - reads (of READS_PER_SAMPLE) in which INA bit P+1 was 1

  readCount := mailbox[MB_SAMPLES + roundIdx * COND_COUNT + condIdx]


PRI cond_label(condIdx) : pLabel
' Printable label for a condition.
'
' @param condIdx - condition, COND_C1..COND_C4
' @returns pLabel - address of the label string

  case condIdx
    COND_C1: pLabel := string("C1 TT=%01 OUT low ")
    COND_C2: pLabel := string("C2 TT=%01 OUT high")
    COND_C3: pLabel := string("C3 TT=%00 OUT low ")
    COND_C4: pLabel := string("C4 TT=%00 OUT high")
    other:   pLabel := string("C? unknown        ")


PRI yes_no(bFlag) : pText
' Printable YES / NO for a boolean.
'
' @param bFlag - TRUE or FALSE
' @returns pText - address of "YES" or "NO"

  if bFlag == TRUE
    pText := string("YES")
  else
    pText := string("NO")


PRI print_samples() | condIdx, roundIdx
' Print every raw sample, grouped by condition, in round order.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local condIdx - condition being printed
' @local roundIdx - round being printed

  repeat condIdx from COND_C1 to COND_C4
    repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
      debug("  ", zstr_(cond_label(condIdx)), "  round ", udec_(roundIdx + 1), ": ", udec_(sample_at(roundIdx, condIdx)))


PRI compute_ranges() | condIdx, roundIdx, readCount
' Smallest and largest sample of every condition.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local condIdx - condition being scanned
' @local roundIdx - round being scanned
' @local readCount - the sample under inspection

  repeat condIdx from COND_C1 to COND_C4
    sample_min[condIdx] := sample_at(0, condIdx)
    sample_max[condIdx] := sample_min[condIdx]
    repeat roundIdx from 1 to ROUNDS - 1
      readCount := sample_at(roundIdx, condIdx)
      if readCount < sample_min[condIdx]
        sample_min[condIdx] := readCount
      if readCount > sample_max[condIdx]
        sample_max[condIdx] := readCount


PRI print_ranges() | condIdx
' Print each condition's range over its ROUNDS samples.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local condIdx - condition being printed

  repeat condIdx from COND_C1 to COND_C4
    debug("  ", zstr_(cond_label(condIdx)), "  min ", udec_(sample_min[condIdx]), "  max ", udec_(sample_max[condIdx]), "  (", udec_(ROUNDS), " samples)")


PRI print_adc_off() | roundIdx
' The OUT-low samples: what the pin's read state carries in the DAC state
' with the ADC off (C1 with TT bit 0 set, C3 with it clear). Informational.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round being printed

  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    debug("  round ", udec_(roundIdx + 1), ":  C1 (TT=%01, OUT low) = ", udec_(sample_at(roundIdx, COND_C1)), "   C3 (TT=%00, OUT low) = ", udec_(sample_at(roundIdx, COND_C3)))
  debug("  C1 range ", udec_(sample_min[COND_C1]), "..", udec_(sample_max[COND_C1]), "   C3 range ", udec_(sample_min[COND_C3]), "..", udec_(sample_max[COND_C3]))
  debug("  C1 separates from C3: ", zstr_(yes_no(separates(COND_C1, COND_C3))), "   C3 separates from C1: ", zstr_(yes_no(separates(COND_C3, COND_C1))), "   (informational, not part of the verdict)")


PRI separates(xCond, yCond) : bSeparates | roundIdx, readCount
' Brief Part 5: X separates from Y when every sample of X lies outside the
' range from the smallest to the largest sample of Y.
'
' @param xCond - condition X
' @param yCond - condition Y
' @returns bSeparates - TRUE when no sample of X lies inside Y's range

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round of the X sample under test
' @local readCount - the X sample under test

  bSeparates := TRUE
  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    readCount := sample_at(roundIdx, xCond)
    if readCount >= sample_min[yCond] and readCount <= sample_max[yCond]
      bSeparates := FALSE
      quit


PRI decide_verdict() | bSep21, bSep43, bSep42
' Run the brief's three separation tests and print the one VERDICT line.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local bSep21 - C2 separates from C1 (the control)
' @local bSep43 - C4 separates from C3
' @local bSep42 - C4 separates from C2

  bSep21 := separates(COND_C2, COND_C1)
  bSep43 := separates(COND_C4, COND_C3)
  bSep42 := separates(COND_C4, COND_C2)
  debug("--- SEPARATION TESTS (X separates from Y: every X sample outside [min Y, max Y]) ---")
  debug("  C2 separates from C1: ", zstr_(yes_no(bSep21)), "   control; YES = the reading sees the ADC at TT = %01")
  debug("  C4 separates from C3: ", zstr_(yes_no(bSep43)), "   prediction NO;  published table YES")
  debug("  C4 separates from C2: ", zstr_(yes_no(bSep42)), "   prediction YES; published table NO")
  debug(" ")
  if bSep21 == FALSE
    debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - C2 does not separate from C1: the neighbour reading does not show the ADC at TT = %01, so C3 and C4 decide nothing (samples above)")
  elseif bSep43 == FALSE and bSep42 == TRUE
    debug("VERDICT: CONFIRMED - at TT = %00 OUT high reads as OUT low (C4 not sep C3) and not as the running ADC (C4 sep C2); at TT = %01 OUT runs the ADC (C2 sep C1)")
    debug("  OUT does not switch the ADC unless TT bit 0 enables the output")
  elseif bSep43 == TRUE and bSep42 == FALSE
    debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - at TT = %00 OUT high separates from OUT low (C4 sep C3) and falls with the running ADC (C4 not sep C2)")
    debug("  OUT enables the ADC at TT = %00, as the published %TT table states")
  elseif bSep43 == TRUE and bSep42 == TRUE
    debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - unpredicted pattern: C4 separates from both C3 and C2 (falls neither with OUT low nor with the running ADC); samples above")
  else
    debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - C4 separates from neither C3 nor C2: the ranges do not discriminate; samples above")


{ MEASURING ENGINE -- runs in its own cog; the ONLY code that touches pins.
  No debug() here (DEBUG_COGS excludes this cog anyway). PTRA = @mailbox on
  entry; PTRB walks the mailbox in the order the MB_ constants list.
}
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Engine ----
engine          mov     ptrb, ptra
                add     ptrb, #MB_K_PRE_HI * 4

                ' observer P+1: A = relative -1 pin's read state, smart pin off,
                ' DIR low for the whole run (never drives)
                dirl    #PIN_NBR
                wrpin   cfg_nbr_, #PIN_NBR
                outl    #PIN_NBR

                call    #path_control           ' K before the rounds

                mov     round_, #ROUNDS
.round          mov     cfg_, cfg_tt01_         ' C1: TT = %01, OUT low
                mov     outlvl_, #OUT_LOW
                call    #do_cond
                mov     outlvl_, #OUT_HIGH      ' C2: TT = %01, OUT high
                call    #do_cond
                mov     cfg_, cfg_tt00_         ' C3: TT = %00, OUT low
                mov     outlvl_, #OUT_LOW
                call    #do_cond
                mov     outlvl_, #OUT_HIGH      ' C4: TT = %00, OUT high
                call    #do_cond
                djnz    round_, #.round

                call    #path_control           ' K after the rounds

                ' leave both pins safe: smart pin off, DIR low, OUT low
                dirl    #PIN_P
                wrpin   #0, #PIN_P
                outl    #PIN_P
                dirl    #PIN_NBR
                wrpin   #0, #PIN_NBR
                outl    #PIN_NBR
                wrlong  #MBOX_DONE, ptra        ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   self_id_
                cogstop self_id_

' Control K: pin P as a plain pin (smart pin off, DIR enables the output),
' one sample driven high, one driven low.
path_control    dirl    #PIN_P
                wrpin   #0, #PIN_P
                drvh    #PIN_P                  ' DIR = 1, OUT = 1
                call    #sample
                drvl    #PIN_P                  ' DIR = 1, OUT = 0
                call    #sample
                ret

' One condition: reset, configure, enable, set OUT, settle, sample.
do_cond         dirl    #PIN_P                  ' configure with DIR low (smart pin in reset)
                wrpin   cfg_, #PIN_P
                dirh    #PIN_P                  ' let the smart pin run
                cmp     outlvl_, #OUT_LOW       wz
        if_z    outl    #PIN_P                  ' OUT set explicitly, whatever came before
        if_nz   outh    #PIN_P
                call    #sample
                ret

' One sample: settle, then READS_PER_SAMPLE reads of INA, counting bit P+1.
sample          waitx   ##SETTLE_CLK
                mov     count_, #0
                rep     #3, reads_
                mov     insnap_, ina
                testb   insnap_, #PIN_NBR       wc
        if_c    add     count_, #1
                wrlong  count_, ptrb
                add     ptrb, #4
                ret

cfg_tt00_       long    CFG_DAC_TT00
cfg_tt01_       long    CFG_DAC_TT01
cfg_nbr_        long    CFG_NBR
reads_          long    READS_PER_SAMPLE

cfg_            res     1               ' WRPIN word for the current condition
outlvl_         res     1               ' OUT_LOW / OUT_HIGH for the current condition
round_          res     1               ' rounds remaining
count_          res     1               ' reads with INA bit P+1 = 1
insnap_         res     1               ' one INA read
self_id_        res     1               ' this cog's id, for COGSTOP

